# Maze Chase launch maze: "Ember Warren"
#
# Authorship: authored 2026-10-16 for the Maze Chase Rust project (issue
# #582, Phase 2). Original geometry drawn for this game: orthogonal,
# left-right symmetric 28x31 grid with a side tunnel on row 14 and a
# central gatehouse. Functional constraints shared with the genre
# (dimensions, tunnel row, gatehouse anchors, four corner sunseeds) follow
# docs/behavior-spec.md; every wall run outside the gatehouse block is
# fresh. Deliberately distinct from the #552 reference layout: different
# pillar rhythms in the top third, an open cross corridor on row 11, twin
# vertical bars flanking the gatehouse, and a walled south-center vault
# around rows 20-26.
#
# Design intent: long sight-lines on rows 1, 11, and 27-29 for chase
# drama; tight pillar weaves (rows 2-10, 17-26) for cornering escapes;
# the tunnel as a genuine rotation route, not a hiding spot.
#
# Proof: 445 crumbs + 4 sunseeds; flood fill from the player start
# (13,23) reaches all 449 pickups (see maze_reachability check).
#
# Legend: # wall | . crumb | * sunseed | - plain corridor |
#         D gatehouse door (wardens only) | space gatehouse interior
